<task id="023" project="spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-15 + §10.1 item 3: Run admin endpoints (list/detail by stage and status, held and dead-lettered runs) and DLQ re-drive wiring the existing DeadLetterQueueService</title>
    <phase>1 Pipeline core and first doors</phase>
    <gate>after:013,011</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags bff-api and authorization; adds admin endpoints (.cs) that re-drive queue work.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Admin endpoints copied from `Api/Admin/JobsEndpoints.cs` (SystemAdmin policy) over an existing, unused service; closed contract. The safety rule (no re-drive of a terminal run) is explicit.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P1-D</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>file-overlap with tasks 017 and 024 on Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs (one Map line each).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>013, 011</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, endpoints, authorization, worker, job</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add an admin-only endpoint group beside `Api/Admin/JobsEndpoints.cs` that lists intake runs by stage and status, shows one run with its admin-attention text, lists dead-lettered intake run messages, and re-drives selected ones through the existing `DeadLetterQueueService` (registered in `WorkersModule.cs:37`, no caller today). A re-drive of a run that is already terminal is refused; a re-driven run resumes from stored state (013) without re-running completed AI stages.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs, Azure Service Bus dead-lettering and ADR-004 job semantics. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`IntakeRunsAdminEndpoints` under `/api/admin/intake` (runs list, run detail, DLQ list, DLQ re-drive) behind `RequireAuthorization("SystemAdmin")`, the first production caller of `DeadLetterQueueService`, unit tests, and the admin guide updated.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-15 (a–c), NFR-06; design §10.1 item 3 (owner: Phase 1). Reuse-scan row 13: extend `Api/Admin` and wire the existing service. `notes/section10-verification-2026-11-25.md` §3: `DeadLetterQueueService.cs` (488 LOC) has `GetSummaryAsync`, `ListMessagesAsync` (:97), `GetMessageAsync` (:153), `RedriveMessagesAsync` (:182); models in `Models/Jobs/DlqModels.cs` (`DlqMessage` carries `RawBody`). Run records and the re-drive marker come from 011; resume and terminal-state semantics from 013.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Admin/IntakeRunsAdminEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Admin/IntakeRunsAdminEndpointsContractTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs (beside `app.MapAdminJobsEndpoints()` :515)</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/guides/BACKGROUND-JOBS-ADMIN-GUIDE.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Admin/JobsEndpoints.cs (MapGroup :57, RequireAuthorization("SystemAdmin") :58, WithName/ProblemDetails shape)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/DeadLetterQueueService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Models/Jobs/DlqModels.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/Admin/JobsEndpointsTests.cs (grandfathered; copy its cases, put the new file under the KEEP path)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="013" status="pending">Orchestrator job type name, terminal states, resume-from-stored-state, admin-attention text.</dependency>
      <dependency task="011" status="pending">sprk_processingjob intake columns (request lookup, stages, re-drive marker).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">SCOPE = every route in the new group. `RequireAuthorization("SystemAdmin")` on the group, as `JobsEndpoints.cs:58`; no per-route override, no anonymous route.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">SCOPE = re-drive. Only messages whose JobType is the intake orchestrator's are listed or re-driven; before re-driving, read the run and refuse (409 INTAKE_RUN_TERMINAL) when it is Completed, Rejected or otherwise terminal; record the re-drive marker on the run (011) before calling `RedriveMessagesAsync`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-017">SCOPE = the run list/detail. Read from the persisted run record (`sprk_processingjob`, job type "Intake run"); never from the Office job-status store; never return Office runs (FR-06 b).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">SCOPE = every response and log. Return ids, stages, statuses, timestamps, error codes and admin-attention text only; never `DlqMessage.RawBody`, payload contents or document text.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">SCOPE = every non-2xx. ProblemDetails with stable `errorCode` (INTAKE_RUN_NOT_FOUND, INTAKE_RUN_TERMINAL, INTAKE_DLQ_MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND, INTAKE_DLQ_UNAVAILABLE).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">Scope: DLQ coverage (owner direction 2026-11-25, consistency). Intake work dead-letters on three queues: the BFF jobs queue (orchestrator and timeout handlers), the engine request queue `intake-engine-requests`, and the engine completion queue `intake-engine-completions` (completion processor, including `WrongQueue`) (task 001 uses the same reason codes: `InvalidFormat`, `Poisoned`, `MaxRetriesExceeded`, `ProcessingError`). Extend the existing `DeadLetterQueueService` with an optional queue name, validated against a closed allow-list from configuration (the BFF jobs queue and the two engine queues; the default is today's queue, so existing behaviour is unchanged). The admin DLQ list and re-drive cover all three queues; a `WrongQueue` message is listed but never re-driven onto a BFF queue. No second registration and no new service.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">SCOPE = DI. Use the existing `DeadLetterQueueService` registration; add no new registration for it and no interface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE.md-§10">SCOPE = this task's BFF changes. State the Placement Justification in the PR (`.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`); measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build (total ≤ 60 MB); no new package, no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

