  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Load the knowledge files and 013/011 outputs; declare RIGOR FULL, tier sonnet, effort high.</step>
    <step order="2">Write `IntakeRunsAdminEndpoints.MapAdminIntakeRunsEndpoints`: `GET /api/admin/intake/runs?stage=&amp;status=&amp;top=` (paged, newest first), `GET /api/admin/intake/runs/{runId}`, `GET /api/admin/intake/dlq` (intake job types only, RawBody stripped), `POST /api/admin/intake/dlq/redrive` body `{ "sequenceNumbers": [..] }`.</step>
    <step order="3">Re-drive: for each sequence number, read the message's job info, resolve the run, refuse terminal runs (per-item result `refused: INTAKE_RUN_TERMINAL`), mark the run, then call `RedriveMessagesAsync` for the accepted set; return per-item outcomes.</step>
    <step order="4">Register the map call beside `MapAdminJobsEndpoints()`; update `BACKGROUND-JOBS-ADMIN-GUIDE.md` with the intake section.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests per the criteria (copy `JobsEndpointsTests.cs` structure); build and run tests; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="7">Document deviations in projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If extending `DeadLetterQueueService` to the engine queue (see the constraint "engine queue DLQ") would change existing callers' behaviour or its public contract beyond an optional queue parameter, STOP and escalate rather than adding a second service instance or registration.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the owner expects an admin UI (not only endpoints) for FR-15, STOP and escalate; a UI is not in this task.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>notes/reuse-scan.md row 13: `Api/Admin/JobsEndpoints.cs:54` covers scheduled jobs only; `DeadLetterQueueService.cs:14` is registered (`WorkersModule.cs:37`) with no caller (section10-verification §3). CAPABILITY-INDEX row 6 (jobs framework).</existing>
    <extension>Yes, extended: a sibling group in `Api/Admin` with the same policy, and the existing service is wired rather than replaced. It is not added inside `JobsEndpoints.cs` because that group serves `Spaarke.Scheduling` jobs (`/api/admin/jobs/{jobId}`), a different id space.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Held or dead-lettered intake runs are invisible and can only be recovered by hand in Service Bus, and the registered DLQ service stays dead code (§10.1 item 3).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
  </tools>

