    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Admin/IntakeRunsAdminEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Admin/IntakeRunsAdminEndpointsContractTests.cs</output>
    <output type="docs">docs/guides/BACKGROUND-JOBS-ADMIN-GUIDE.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A SystemAdmin caller can list intake runs filtered by stage and status and open one run with its stages and admin-attention text; Office runs never appear.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The DLQ list returns only intake orchestrator messages, with job ids, run ids, reason and delivery count, and no RawBody or payload content.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Re-driving a dead-lettered, non-terminal run calls `RedriveMessagesAsync` for it, marks the run, and the run resumes from stored state without re-running completed AI stages (FR-15 b, verified with 013's resume test double).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: re-driving a terminal run is refused with INTAKE_RUN_TERMINAL and nothing is re-driven (FR-15 c).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a non-admin caller gets 403 and an unauthenticated caller 401 on every route (FR-15 a); an unknown run id → 404 INTAKE_RUN_NOT_FOUND; an unknown sequence number → per-item INTAKE_DLQ_MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`DeadLetterQueueService` has a production caller and no new DI registration was added for it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build and all tests pass; the PR states the Placement Justification and publish-size delta (≤ 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE). Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the negative cases named above; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes. One seeding proof for the terminal-run refusal.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>FR-15; §10.1 item 3. Scope is intake runs; a general DLQ view for every job type is not added (file a follow-up with `/project-defer-issue-tracking` if wanted). Folder `Api/Admin/` per the brief ("extend Api/Admin").</notes>

